{
  "case_id": "2008-08-214",
  "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:18 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Atlantic Sounding Co., Inc.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Townsend is a Jones Act seaman who seeks punitive damages for the willful failure to pay maintenance and cure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Atlantic Sounding Co., Inc.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Townsend cannot recover punitive damages under his general maritime law cause of action because those damages are unavailable under the Jones Act FELA, and to a lesser extent DOHSA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David W. McCreadie",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCREADIE: Yes, Justice Ginsburg, there is a remedy. And that's what Vaughan v. Atkinson provides. In that case this Court looked at abuse of the litigation process and determined that the plaintiff in that case was entitled to attorneys' fees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Is any of them called punitive damages? Do you know of any case in which a court has --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David W. McCreadie",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCREADIE: No. The dissent mentioned that. But you can not speak for the majority opinion. But up until Vaughan v. Atkinson, in the history of the United States there was never a holding where punitive damages were awarded to a Jones Act seaman for the failure to pay maintenance and cure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: As I read your reply brief -- and please correct me if it's a misimpression -- you didn't dispute the fact that punitive damages were available historically for the shipowner's wrongful refusal to provide maintenance and cure, or am I wrong about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We're much more comfortable relying on this\nCourt's precedents, the line of cases that builds from\nMoragne to Higgingbotham and culminates in Miles, we're\nmuch more comfortable looking at the history of the\ndamages awarded by this Court to seamen, where it uses\nthe term compensatory damages -- compensation for --\nover and over and over without any mention whatsoever of\npunitive damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now our position here is that a seaman\nshould be not ever have to come before a court to seek\nmaintenance and cure, and the court should never, ever\nhave to award punitive damages."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How many of these seamen\nwho seek maintenance and cure are represented? I mean,\nwhat is the incidence of representation for maintenance\nand cure claims as distinguished from Jones Act\nnegligence type claims with the -- the possibility of\nlarge recoveries for pain and suffering?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "punitive damages were part of the common law until taken\naway by Congress.\nAnd -- and it could be asserted that\nmaintenance and cure punitive damages were not necessary\nbecause the threat was enough to -- to require\nshipowners to go ahead and provide this. And I would\npoint out to the Court that this had not been a problem\nprior to Guevara. Shipowners did self-regulate. They\ndidn't -- seamen didn't run to the courts every time\nthey wanted maintenance and cure; whereas, today they\nhave to."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SULLIVAN",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SULLIVAN: I think this would be different because all we're talking about is does the seaman get the surgery he needs. If he doesn't get the surgery he needs and he gets worse or continues to stay ill or he continues to stay in pain, then the ship owner should be punished."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. SULLIVAN",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SULLIVAN: The goal here, Judge, is not money. The goal here, I think --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, I mean, it -- whether it gives rise to more litigation or not, it is still a significant and will give rise to greater costs on the part of the shipper which will be passed on, as is the case in a lot of areas where you have punitive damages, it will be passed on to the consumer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-214",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4445e81a6974b73317ea0e495414736e656a40846f7a6f0b3cdfd1eaecde1577",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4445e81a6974-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
